<title>FINLAND: SKANSKA PARTNER IN FINNISH HOTEL REBUILD.</title>
<headline>SKANSKA PARTNER IN FINNISH HOTEL REBUILD.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Skanska's subsidiary Skanska Etela-Suomi Oy and Rakennus Oy Leo Heinanen will rebuild a Merita building in central Helsinki to a hotel, Merita said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The value of the total investment is 250 million markka,&quot; Merita said but did not specify how much of this was for the joint venture involving Skanska.</p>
<p>The famous Kamp hotel building which for long served as banking headquarters will be rebuilt to a hotel to he run by U.S. hotel company ITT Sheraton , Merita said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
